    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5431": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Visiting Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Visiting Assistant Professor Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For other document 1, please upload a document with the name and contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00643 Position Title: Visiting Assistant Professor Local Title: Visiting Assistant Professor Job Category Faculty FLSA Classification: Obligation: Academic Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: Position Type Temporary Appointment Start date: 09/01/2026 Appointment End date : 08/31/2027 Salary: $60,000 - $70,000 Salary Grade: Full Time or Part Time: Full Time If Part-Time, fill in %: Benefits Summary UUP Full-time Benefits Summary Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Department Information Department: PSYCHOLOGY Division Academic Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Heather Beauchamp Search Contact Phone/Extension: 315-244-2017 Search Contact Email: beauchhm@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: The Department of Psychology at SUNY Potsdam invites applications for a Visiting Assistant Professor position, to begin Fall 2026. The area of specialization is Counseling/Clinical/School Psychology. This position is open until filled. Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: The successful applicant will be prepared to teach a variety of courses within their area of specialization (i.e., Counseling Theories & Methods, Abnormal Psychology, etc.). The position will be .75 teaching and .25 Counseling Center service. Required Qualifications: PhD in Psychology or master’s degree with more than two years of Counseling/Clinical experience. We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with an increasingly diverse array of students and colleagues and who have demonstrated a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. Preferred Qualifications: Special preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching such courses as Abnormal Psychology, Forensic Psychology, Counseling Theories and Methods, and Drugs and Behavior at the college level. We are, especially, seeking candidates who have worked with, done research with, or taught under-represented groups and have worked collaboratively across various departments in fostering success of underrepresented groups. Supervisor: H. Beauchamp Location: Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: For other document 1, please upload a document with the name and contact information for three professional references. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) * If you heard about this job posting on social media, please indicate what platform: Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Other Not Applicable Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New York at Potsdam, all rights reserved. 44 Pierrepont Avenue | Potsdam, NY 13676 | 315-267-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
